IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`
IMPORT `vmu-s06-s07-notification-and-calculation`

-- Tests of sections 6 and 7.
-- Each expected value is worked out by hand from the quoted line above it.

§ `Section 6 -- Notification of values of fee and penalty units`

-- src:67 | Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of—
-- src:68 | (a) the value of the fee unit that is to apply for the financial year commencing on 1 July in that year; and
-- src:69 | (b) the value of the penalty unit that is to apply for the financial year commencing on 1 July in that year.
-- Arguments in order: the year; the day of publication in the Gazette; the day of publication in a newspaper; the newspaper circulates generally throughout Victoria;
-- the notice states the value of the fee unit; the notice states the value of the penalty unit.
-- Everything in order, on 31 May, the day before 1 June.
#ASSERT     `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 31 5 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Everything in order, earlier.
#ASSERT     `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 1 5 2025) (Date 15 5 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- On 1 June itself, in the Gazette or in the newspaper, or on 2 June: too late.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 31 5 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 2 6 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A newspaper that does not circulate generally throughout Victoria, or a notice that leaves out one of the two values, does not meet the section.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 31 5 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 31 5 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2025 (Date 31 5 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The year matters: dates in May 2025 are not before 1 June 2024.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` 2024 (Date 31 5 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 7 -- Calculation of a fee or penalty`

-- src:73 | (1) The amount of a fee provided for by an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument by a fee unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of fee units applicable by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5.
-- An Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument: 3.5 fee units at 12.53 dollars is 43.855 dollars.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `an Act` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.855
#ASSERT `s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `a statutory rule` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.855
#ASSERT `s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `a legislative instrument` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.855
-- Any other kind of instrument: the text gives no rule.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `an instrument of another kind` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:74 | (2) The amount of a penalty provided for by an Act or statutory rule by a penalty unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of penalty units applicable by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5.
-- An Act or a statutory rule: 2 penalty units at 140.84 dollars is 281.68 dollars.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `an Act` 2 140.84 EQUALS JUST 281.68
#ASSERT `s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `a statutory rule` 2 140.84 EQUALS JUST 281.68
-- A legislative instrument is not named in subsection (2), nor is any other kind: no rule.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `a legislative instrument` 2 140.84 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `an instrument of another kind` 2 140.84 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:75 | (3) The amount of a fee calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
-- "may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents": 43.855 to 43.90; with 0.5 fee units at 12.53 dollars, 6.265 is nearer 6.30 than 6.20 (0.035 against 0.065), so 6.3.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `an Act` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.9
#ASSERT `s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `a legislative instrument` 0.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 6.3
-- 1 fee unit at 12.55 dollars is exactly half way between 12.50 and 12.60: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `an Act` 1 12.55 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Another kind of instrument: no calculation, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `an instrument of another kind` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:76 | (4) The amount of a penalty calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest dollar.
-- "may be rounded to the nearest dollar": 281.68 to 282; 1.5 penalty units at 140.84 is 211.26, to 211.
#ASSERT `s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `an Act` 2 140.84 EQUALS JUST 282
#ASSERT `s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `a statutory rule` 1.5 140.84 EQUALS JUST 211
-- 1 penalty unit at 140.5 dollars is exactly half way between 140 and 141: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `an Act` 1 140.5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A legislative instrument has no calculation under subsection (2), so none to round.
#ASSERT `s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7 may be rounded` `a legislative instrument` 2 140.84 EQUALS NOTHING
